WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:16.235
Wyssa snatched the ring from the contraption she'd built.

2
00:00:16.235 --> 00:00:20.997
"Don't worry," she said. "I'll deal with Morb."

3
00:00:20.998 --> 00:00:24.602
She stomped off, but Zann and the others caught up with her.

4
00:00:24.602 --> 00:00:26.904
"We're coming too," Zann said.

5
00:00:26.905 --> 00:00:29.612
"No." Wyssa shoved him aside.

6
00:00:29.612 --> 00:00:33.959
"It's my responsibility. Now get out of my way."

7
00:00:33.959 --> 00:00:37.205
"But we want to help!" Saffa said.

8
00:00:37.206 --> 00:00:42.378
"Yeah," Perda said. "Besides, you can't just leave us here.

9
00:00:42.378 --> 00:00:46.223
We might not be able to find our way back to Magica without you.

10
00:00:46.223 --> 00:00:49.310
Morb took our guidelink, remember?"

11
00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:56.157
Darb nodded. "And even if we do find our way back, First City isn't safe for us right now."

12
00:00:56.157 --> 00:01:00.953
"That's fine," Wyssa said. "Atmo is pleasant and safe.

13
00:01:00.953 --> 00:01:06.815
You can relax here, and I'll return for you once I'm done with Morb."

14
00:01:06.815 --> 00:01:10.721
Saffa nodded. "Perhaps that's for the best."

15
00:01:10.721 --> 00:01:14.643
"No!" Zann cried. "You can't leave us here!"

16
00:01:14.643 --> 00:01:18.657
"Yeah, what if you need our help?" Perda exclaimed.

17
00:01:18.657 --> 00:01:21.311
Wyssa's eyebrows shot up in surprise.

18
00:01:21.312 --> 00:01:23.564
"What?" she cried.

19
00:01:23.564 --> 00:01:30.548
"I don't require help from anyone, especially a bunch of chattering children."

20
00:01:30.548 --> 00:01:33.697
"You might." Zann didn't back down.

21
00:01:33.697 --> 00:01:37.111
"We were the ones who stopped Morb before, remember?"

22
00:01:37.111 --> 00:01:39.448
"That's right!" Perda chimed in.

23
00:01:39.449 --> 00:01:41.594
"We couldn't have done it without your help.

24
00:01:41.595 --> 00:01:45.337
But you couldn't have done it without our help either."

25
00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:48.479
"The kids have a point," Saffa said.

26
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:53.322
"They've done more to stop Morb's terrible plans than anyone."

27
00:01:53.322 --> 00:01:59.393
Wyssa glowered at them all. Finally she shrugged. "Fine," she snapped.

28
00:01:59.394 --> 00:02:02.266
"But I'm not babysitting any of you, all right?

29
00:02:02.266 --> 00:02:08.162
Now let's go. I need to gather more ingredients on our way back."

30
00:02:08.162 --> 00:02:12.441
She grabbed more twigs and plants on the way to the Atmo wormhole.

31
00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:19.224
But she didn't stop there. Once they were in the vortex, she led the way into world after world.

32
00:02:19.225 --> 00:02:25.725
Zann and his friends had visited a few of the worlds before, but there were several that they'd never seen.

33
00:02:25.725 --> 00:02:31.379
They stayed in each one just long enough for Wyssa to gather a few ingredients.

34
00:02:31.379 --> 00:02:40.095
Zann and his friends barely had time to rest and recover their magic energy before they were zooming through the vortex again.

35
00:02:40.096 --> 00:02:45.465
After landing in one world, Zann felt weak and out of breath.

36
00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:50.463
He breathed deeply, and right away he regretted it.

37
00:02:50.463 --> 00:02:55.231
"Ugh," Perda exclaimed. "We're back in Niffia!"

38
00:02:55.231 --> 00:02:58.447
"Oh my!" Saffa looked startled.

39
00:02:58.447 --> 00:03:04.338
"I've read about this place, but the stench is worse than I ever could have imagined!"

40
00:03:04.338 --> 00:03:06.968
"Definitely," Gliss agreed.

41
00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:09.132
"Hush," Wyssa scolded.

42
00:03:09.132 --> 00:03:15.165
"Here come our hosts. Don't embarrass me by insulting their lovely world."

43
00:03:15.166 --> 00:03:21.733
Zann rolled his eyes. Niffia might look lovely, but it sure didn't smell lovely!

44
00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:29.110
As usual, a greeting committee was hurrying toward them with big smiles on their faces, which lacked noses.

45
00:03:29.111 --> 00:03:33.834
"Greetings, dear friend!" one of the Niffians cried, beaming at Wyssa.

46
00:03:33.835 --> 00:03:37.589
"It's an honor as always to have you here!"

47
00:03:37.589 --> 00:03:40.724
"Thank you, my friends." Wyssa smiled.

48
00:03:40.724 --> 00:03:46.128
"With your permission I'm here to gather some ingredients for a spell."

49
00:03:46.128 --> 00:03:49.877
"Of course—everything we have is yours."

50
00:03:49.878 --> 00:03:56.228
A Niffian waved toward the fields and forests surrounding them. "Please help yourself."

51
00:03:56.228 --> 00:03:58.667
"Thank you." Wyssa bowed.

52
00:03:58.668 --> 00:04:05.767
"While I'm gathering what I need, perhaps you would be so kind as to look after my friends?"

53
00:04:05.768 --> 00:04:11.587
"It would be our honor," another Niffian assured her, bowing to the kids and Saffa.

54
00:04:11.587 --> 00:04:16.464
"Come with us for some rest and refreshment."

55
00:04:16.464 --> 00:04:24.962
Zann and the others did their best to ignore the smell as the Niffians took them back to their town and gave them food and drink.

56
00:04:24.962 --> 00:04:28.437
"This world would be perfect if it didn't stink!"

57
00:04:28.438 --> 00:04:31.810
Zann whispered to Darb when the Niffians weren't listening.

58
00:04:31.811 --> 00:04:35.825
"And Morb might be perfect if he wasn't evil," Darb replied.

59
00:04:35.825 --> 00:04:38.827
"I wonder what he's doing in the Far Frontier."

60
00:04:38.827 --> 00:04:42.456
Zann shrugged. "Look, here comes Wyssa."

61
00:04:42.456 --> 00:04:46.135
Wyssa hurried over. The Niffians rushed to greet her.

62
00:04:46.135 --> 00:04:50.863
"I trust you found what you needed, my friend?" one of them asked.

63
00:04:50.863 --> 00:04:54.728
"I did indeed." She smiled and bowed.

64
00:04:54.728 --> 00:04:58.237
Then she turned to survey Zann and the others.

65
00:04:58.237 --> 00:05:00.952
"You look comfortable," she said.

66
00:05:00.952 --> 00:05:06.943
"Perhaps you should stay here while I, er, take care of things back in Magica."

67
00:05:06.943 --> 00:05:13.749
"No!" Zann blurted out, horrified at the thought of being stuck in stinky Niffia for a long time.

68
00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:16.272
"You promised we could come with you."

69
00:05:16.272 --> 00:05:20.143
"I promised no such thing," Wyssa retorted.

70
00:05:20.143 --> 00:05:23.850
Meanwhile the Niffians looked even happier than usual.

71
00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:28.923
"It would be our honor if you stayed!" one of them exclaimed.

72
00:05:28.923 --> 00:05:31.178
"Yes," another added.

73
00:05:31.179 --> 00:05:35.717
"That would give you a chance to see even more of our beautiful world!"

74
00:05:35.717 --> 00:05:43.553
"We can't stay," Zann said, trying desperately to think of a way to convince Wyssa not to leave them behind.

75
00:05:43.553 --> 00:05:46.028
"Wyssa needs our help."

76
00:05:46.029 --> 00:05:53.613
"Yeah, we haven't even had a chance to tell you about everything else that's happening in Magica," Perda told Wyssa.

77
00:05:53.613 --> 00:05:56.906
"Like what?" Wyssa sounded skeptical.

78
00:05:56.907 --> 00:06:04.784
"Like you shouldn't just go barging back into Magica without knowing that the king and queen quit and disappeared," Gliss said.

79
00:06:04.784 --> 00:06:11.390
Wyssa raised one eyebrow. "Interesting. But not relevant."

80
00:06:11.391 --> 00:06:17.416
"And how about Zann's parents being accused of stealing those missing relics?" Perda added.

81
00:06:17.416 --> 00:06:23.644
"Missing relics?" This time Wyssa's voice was sharper. "What missing relics?"

82
00:06:23.644 --> 00:06:25.036
Zann shrugged.

83
00:06:25.036 --> 00:06:30.963
"A few of the things in the lab disappeared, and nobody knows where they went or who took them," he said.

84
00:06:30.963 --> 00:06:33.349
"Like the Mask of Zanta, and—"

85
00:06:33.349 --> 00:06:36.692
"All right, that's enough chatter,” Wyssa interrupted.

86
00:06:36.707 --> 00:06:40.275
“I've changed my mind. You're coming with me."

87
00:06:40.275 --> 00:06:42.675
She bowed quickly to the Niffians.

88
00:06:42.675 --> 00:06:47.506
"Thanks again, my friends. We must depart."

89
00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:51.238
Moments later the whole group was back in the vortex.

90
00:06:51.239 --> 00:06:57.792
Zann was relieved. But why had Wyssa changed her mind so abruptly after hearing about the relics?

91
00:06:57.793 --> 00:07:02.275
Before he could ask, he saw a wormhole spinning toward them up ahead.

92
00:07:02.275 --> 00:07:09.759
"Hang on," Wyssa called, yanking them toward it. "We're here."
